    "englishTranslation": "First Chapter (Prathamaḥ Paricchedaḥ). Advaitasiddhi composed by Śrī Madhusūdana Sarasvatī.\n\n1. All-glorious is Viṣṇu (the all-pervading Pure Consciousness), free from all conceptual constructions, who is the substratum of the illusory universe of duality headed by Maya-fashioned knowership, whose essence is Truth, Knowledge, and Bliss, who is intuited by the indivisible non-relational cognition arisen from the crown of the Vedas (the Upaniṣads), and who—as though having cast off illusory bondage—shines supreme in liberation of the nature of unbroken Supreme Bliss.\n2. Salutations to the sacred dust arisen from the feet of Śrī Rāma (Tīrtha), Viśveśvara (Sarasvatī), and Mādhava (Sarasvatī), who realized Mādhava (the Supreme Lord) through absolute non-dual identity, and by whose touch the impurities of tamas and rajas are dispelled.\n3. Vast and boundless treatises composed by many sages for the welfare of others flourish supreme; this labor of mine, however, will surely serve here to cultivate my own inner fulfillment.\n4. May this Advaitasiddhi, composed with utmost diligence by the sage Madhusūdana—whose sole wealth is faith—after synthesizing the entire ocean of scriptures, bring delight to the wise for rapid illumination and triumph over opponents.",
